What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/poc-version/<dev>
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	5.15
Contact:	Navid Jalali <navidcity@gmail.com>
Description:
		The poc-version driver binds to every Instance of the PoC
		library's Version Register IP core
		(PoC.axi4lite_GitVersionRegister) that the device tree
		describes with the compatible string
		"plc2,poc-git-version-register". Each Instance is a
		separate platform device <dev>, and the driver directory
		holds one symbolic link per bound Instance, named after the
		device (for example "a0010000.version"). The same device is
		also reachable as /sys/bus/platform/devices/<dev>. The
		driver directory also holds entries that are not Instances
		(bind, unbind, uevent, module); only Instances have a
		common/ directory.

		A design may contain any number of Instances. All of them
		are found the same way, for example::

		  for dev in /sys/bus/platform/drivers/poc-version/*/; do
		      [ -d "${dev}common" ] || continue
		      cat "${dev}common/build_date"
		  done

		Each Instance has three Category directories, common/, top/
		and uid/, with one file per Value. The files of an Instance
		reflect only that Instance's Registers.

		Rules that apply to every Value file below:

		- The files are read-only (mode 0444). Nothing written
		  through sysfs can change what the driver reports.
		- Each file holds one Formatted value followed by a single
		  newline ("\n").
		- Values are read from the Instance's Cached copy, which is
		  filled from the hardware once, when the Instance is
		  probed. Reading a file never accesses the hardware.
		- A file is absent when the active Register layout of the
		  Instance lacks that Value. The presence of a file means
		  the Value exists. Which layout is active is given by
		  common/version_of_version_reg. The three Category
		  directories always exist for a bound Instance, even when
		  the active layout has no Value in one of them; such a
		  directory is then empty.
		- An Instance whose Version-of-Version-Reg the driver does
		  not know is not bound: probe fails with -ENODEV and logs
		  the Version-of-Version-Reg. Such an Instance has no
		  Category directories and no files at all. Today only
		  Register layout 1 is known.
		- Values are shown as they are, without checking whether
		  they make sense. Implausible contents (for example month
		  13, or non-printable bytes in a string) are printed as
		  they are.
		- Decimal numbers have no leading zeros unless stated.
		  Hex digits are lower case and have no "0x" prefix.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/poc-version/<dev>/common/build_date
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	5.15
Contact:	Navid Jalali <navidcity@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RO) Build date of the FPGA design, from Common.BuildDate,
		as an ISO 8601 date::

		  YYYY-MM-DD\n

		The year is zero-padded to at least four digits, the month
		and the day to at least two.

		Present in Register layout 1.

		Example::

		  2026-10-27

What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/poc-version/<dev>/common/version_of_version_reg
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	5.15
Contact:	Navid Jalali <navidcity@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RO) Version-of-Version-Reg: the unsigned decimal number in
		the low byte of Common.NumberModule_VersionOfVersionReg. It
		says which Register layout the Instance uses. The upper bits
		of that Register are not shown. Format::

		  <n>\n

		Present in Register layout 1.

		Example (Register layout 1)::

		  1

What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/poc-version/<dev>/common/vivado_version
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	5.15
Contact:	Navid Jalali <navidcity@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RO) Version of the Vivado toolchain that built the design,
		from Common.VivadoVersion, as three unsigned decimal
		numbers::

		  Major.Minor.Patch\n

		Present in Register layout 1.

		Example::

		  2024.2.0

What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/poc-version/<dev>/common/project_name
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	5.15
Contact:	Navid Jalali <navidcity@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RO) Project name of the FPGA design, from the 20-byte
		Common.ProjectName block, as text::

		  <text>\n

		The text stops at the first null byte and never goes beyond
		the 20-byte block, so it is 0 to 20 bytes long. An empty
		name reads as just "\n". Bytes are printed as they are.

		Present in Register layout 1.

		Example::

		  my_board_design

What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/poc-version/<dev>/top/version
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	5.15
Contact:	Navid Jalali <navidcity@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RO) Version of the top-level FPGA design that contains the
		Instance, from Top.Version::

		  major.minor.patch[+N][ dirty][ untracked]\n

		major, minor and patch are unsigned decimal numbers.
		Optional parts, in this order:

		- "+N" when the build is N commits after the tag (N is
		  the 6-bit commits-to-tag Field, unsigned decimal, 1 to
		  63). Omitted when N is 0.
		- " dirty" (with a leading space) when the Dirty_modified
		  bit is set: the working tree had modified files.
		- " untracked" (with a leading space) when the
		  Dirty_untracked bit is set: the working tree had
		  untracked files.

		Present in Register layout 1.

		Examples::

		  1.4.0
		  1.4.0+3
		  2.10.5+63
		  1.4.0 dirty
		  1.4.0 untracked
		  1.4.0 dirty untracked
		  1.4.0+3 dirty untracked

What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/poc-version/<dev>/top/git_hash
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	5.15
Contact:	Navid Jalali <navidcity@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RO) Git commit hash of the top-level design, from the
		20-byte Top.GitHash block, as a hex integer of exactly 40
		lower-case hex digits without "0x"::

		  <40 hex digits>\n

		The IP core stores the hash reversed. The file shows it in
		normal commit order, as Git prints it, so it can be passed
		straight to "git show".

		Present in Register layout 1.

		Example::

		  bc91981278b2611b0b12dd09bf1a2d8f74f0b8ed

